emma\u202f4 demonstrates that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) can indeed be achieved.  \nConsequently, for any integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) the set of possible numbers of sunny lines is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\,\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}\\,}.\n\\]"
