blem and having exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.  \nThe collinearity Lemma\u202f1 proves that no configuration can have more than \\(n\\) sunny lines, and the trivial lower bound \\(k\\ge 0\\) is obvious.  \n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]"
